th in the UK: a longitudinal, Bayesian quasi-experimental analysis\". <em>BMJ Mental Health<\/em><br><a class=\"btn btn-outline-dark btn-sm\" href=\"https://mentalhealth.bmj.com/content/29/1/e302688\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-file-pdf\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Publication\"><\/i> Publication<\/a>    <a class=\"btn btn-outline-dark btn-sm\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjment-2026-302688\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><i class=\"ai ai-doi-square\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"DOI\"><\/i> DOI<\/a> <a class=\"btn btn-outline-dark btn-sm\" href=\"/publications/bib/jefferyal-2026.bib\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-quote-left\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cite\"><\/i> Cite<\/a>","A Gabrio, M Daniels, <b>G Baio<\/b>. (2026). \"A Bayesian Approach for Nonignorable Dropout in Bivariate Longitudinal Models\".<br>  <a class=\"btn btn-outline-dark btn-sm\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.25749\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><i class=\"ai ai-arxiv-square\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Arxiv\"><\/i> Arxiv<\/a>   <a class=\"btn btn-outline-dark btn-sm\" href=\"/publications/bib/gabrioetal-2026.bib\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-quote-left\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cite\"><\/i> Cite<\/a>","M Adeleke, G Marra, <b>G Baio<\/b>, AG O'Keeffe. (2026). \"Thin plate regression splines for treatment effect estimation in a local randomisation regression discontinuity design\". <em>Computational Statistics & Data Analysis<\/em><br><a class=\"btn btn-outline-dark btn-sm\" href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0167947325001823\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-file-pdf\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Publication\"><\/i> Publication<\/a>    <a class=\"btn btn-outline-dark btn-sm\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.csda.2025.108306\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><i class=\